##When to use each model

An investigative team with limited analyst capacity should deploy the Random Forest. 
Every flag it raises is confirmed fraud with near certainty. Investigators never 
chase dead leads. The cost is missing roughly 9 out of 100 illicit transactions 
that the GNN would have caught.

A team focused on maximum fraud volume for example, a compliance department 
running automated pre-screening before human review  should use the GNN. It catches 
91 out of 100 illicit transactions. The tradeoff is that roughly half its flags 
require a second look before escalating to an investigator.

The strongest production architecture runs both in sequence. The GNN casts the 
wide net. The Random Forest validates before anything reaches a human desk. 
Together they approach both high recall and high precision simultaneously.
